<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45898" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭb-īrascor</span></b> ,
			ātus, 3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. n.</i>, <i>to be
				somewhat angry</i> (Ciceronian): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">interdum soleo subirasci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 2, 4, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">brevitati litterarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 11, 24, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in Epirum quod me non invitas, subirascor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 9, 7, 7</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭbīrātus</span></b> , a,
			um, P. a., <i>somewhat angry</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tibi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					de Or. 1, 16, 72</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Fam. 3, 9, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anus subiratior,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 4, p. 154</span></i>
			 (dub. al. iratior).</div>
